nces generally **$20–$250** on Plus/Pro, with larger amounts possible under Builder; standard delivery is free, while same-day delivery currently runs roughly **$4.49–$14.99**. citeturn303536search4turn303536search5\n- **Current** — worth checking especially if you already use or are willing to use their banking product.\n- **Chime** — SpotMe/MyPay can serve essentially the same purpose if you meet their direct-deposit/account requirements.\n- **Tilt** — formerly Empower; currently advertises cash advances up to around **$500**, though there's an **$8/month** subscription after the trial. citeturn303536search6\n- **Albert** — another large player, though I'd pay attention to the subscription structure before signing up.\n\nFor **your situation**, where the objective sounds like *“I need an extra $50–$300 bridge and I want to know what can actually fund me now,”* I'd probably test them in this order: **MoneyLion → Dave → Klover → Cleo → Current/Chime**, rather than signing up for five monthly subscriptions at once.\n\nOne important thing: approval amounts are **very account-specific**. Two apps advertising $500 can give one person $25 and another person $300 based on recurring deposits, checking-account history, balance patterns, and prior repayment behavior. citeturn303536search13\n\nIf you tell me **roughly how much you're trying to bridge — like $50, $100, $200, or $500 — and whether you have direct deposit**, I can narrow it down to the **2–3 most realistic ones to try tonight**."]}, "create_time": 1790305435.704776, "end_turn": true, "id": "7d976b69-2d4f-4821-b608-72a2114b5f01", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "([NerdWallet](https://www.nerdwallet.com/personal-loans/learn/cash-advance-apps?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 424, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "NerdWallet", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": 1779408000, "refs": [